course: dictionary
lesson: 3863
title: Fragile: easily broken or harmed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fragile means easily broken or damaged. Look at the words around it for clues. A parcel marked «Fragile» must be handled gently, so the label is warning you to take care with what is inside.
explain: «Museum objects can be old and fragile, and touching them can break them forever.» The clue is break them forever, so fragile must mean something that breaks easily. Try your meaning in the sentence: easily broken fits, and it makes sense.
explain: Fragile can also describe a person who is weak, ill or easily upset. Things like peace or nature can be fragile too, meaning they can be harmed easily. Read the sentence «insects have fragile bodies that are easily hurt» and the clue easily hurt shows the same meaning.
fact: Fragile means easily broken or damaged.
fact: «Fragile» on a parcel means handle it gently, as with glass, eggs or china.
fact: In science, fragile ecosystems such as coral reefs are easily harmed by pollution.
fact: A fragile person may be weak, ill or easily upset, and a fragile environment can be easily harmed.
fact: Useful phrases: «fragile glass», «handle with care», «fragile environment».
exercise: «Museum objects can be old and fragile, and touching them can break them forever.» What does fragile mean here? | Very heavy | *Easily broken | Loud and noisy | Brightly coloured
exercise: A parcel has a label that says «Fragile». What should you do? | Drop it on the stairs to test it | *Carry it carefully and handle it gently | Leave it out in the rain | Shake it to see what is inside
exercise: Ella says fragile means strong. Is she right? | No, fragile means very bright | Yes, fragile means very tough | Yes, fragile means very heavy | *No, fragile means easily broken or damaged
test: «Dried tardigrades survive great cold, high pressure and radiation, but active tardigrades are quite fragile.» What does quite fragile suggest about active tardigrades? | They are extremely strong | They never need food | They cannot be seen | *They are easily damaged
test: A child says «fragile» means unbreakable. What is the right meaning? | Unbreakable | *Easily broken or damaged | Sticky | Hidden
exam: Which sentence uses fragile to describe a person who is weak or easily upset? | *«She felt fragile after being ill for so long.» | «The parcel was sent by post.» | «The sun was bright over the sea.» | «The bridge was built from strong steel.»
